        "original_id": "de3e9af3-51c6-54ce-b736-684ac48ab930",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Fabaceae, Iridaceae\n- Places: Australia, tropical Africa, southern Africa\n- People: James Edward Smith, Wayne Cooper\n- Concepts: plant genera, Mirbelioids, fashion design\n- Products: Bossiaea, Ferraria, Platylobium\n\nFacts:\n- Bossiaea is a genus in the pea family Fabaceae with about 70 species native to Australia.\n- Ferraria is a genus of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family Iridaceae native to tropical and southern Africa.\n- James Edward Smith first described the genus Platylobium.\n- Platylobium is closely allied to Bossiaea within the Mirbelioids.\n- Wayne Cooper is a British-born fashion designer based in Australia.",
